# Raw research inputs are re-downloaded by scripts/run_pipeline.py and are
# fingerprinted in data/raw_manifest.json. The one file that cannot be
# re-downloaded (a hand transcription of an official injury report) is kept.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/official_injuries_w10_2026.csv
# Added by session arena-543cdcb0-x1. `data/raw/*` was silently governing the PINNED upstream mirror
# (data/raw/nflverse/*.csv) and the Week 10 official injury transcription: 14 files were tracked while
# matching the ignore rule, so `git add data/raw/nflverse/games.csv` did nothing without `-f`, a
# `git clean -xdf` in any session would have deleted the mirror the results feed and the control
# baselines are cross-checked against, and `git ls-files -i -c` was non-empty on main. Re-included
# explicitly: a pinned, hashed input is evidence, and evidence is not scratch.
!data/raw/nflverse/
!data/raw/nflverse/**
!data/raw/injuries_2026_week10_official.psv
_site/

